  "reasoning": "Assembled from reader's 22-item findings array without dropping or merging any. Core interpretive work: (1) resolved finding #8's doc self-contradiction using §11.1 + actual code as the tiebreaker; (2) used finding #6 to explicitly correct the maintainer's stated historical belief rather than silently accepting it; (3) split the type-system gap into two clusters (build/identity vs. distribution/sink) rather than treating it as one monolithic gap, since the evidence (findings 1-4 vs. 5) supports two distinct closure surfaces; (4) built the tiered recommendation by testing each candidate feature (napi/maturin placement, CLI-binary-to-GHRelease, Homebrew-tap) against the maintainer's stated 'lean on native tools, coordinate don't reimplement' philosophy using findings 9 and 15-17, which produced a clear differentiator: gh CLI exists as a native upload tool but no native tool performs Homebrew formula templating+push, so goreleaser/cargo-dist reimplement it themselves — meaning callisto doing the same would violate its stated identity, not extend it."
